; Wake recovery: what can recover a refused wake. A wake that did not leave
; its seat Awake keeps its work queued, and Flow's records alone decide
; whether it is still due. The refusal keeps the cause it arose from, and
; that cause alone names the recovery.
;
; HerdrUnread names why Herdr could not be read: ServerUnreachable, the
; Herdr CLI did not run or the session's server did not answer it;
; PaneUnreadable, Herdr answered with no readable agent roster.
;
; FreshRefusal names why a fresh wake's launch did not start:
; ConfigurationUnread, the configuration snapshot was not read;
; NoLayerModel, no model is configured for the layer; Rejected, the Start
; was refused with its rejection; Unsettled, the Start was neither refused
; nor seen Started, so its flow may run.
;
; WakeRecovery classes a refusal by its preserved cause. Terminal: waiting
; recovers nothing; the work waits for a change to what the wake reads.
; AwaitingPane: a Herdr agent event on that pane can establish recovery, and
; the wake is tried again on pane.agent_detected or pane.agent_status_changed
; for it. AwaitingServer: a server or endpoint did not answer and no event
; announces its return; the wake is tried again at the next request queued
; for the metaflow or at the Nexus's next start. Reconcile: a flow of the
; metaflow may already run; nothing is launched again, and the next wake
; settles the running flow from Flow's records and Herdr. Unresolved: the
; preserved cause does not show which; the wake is tried again at the next
; request or start.
;
; AgentPaneEvent is one Herdr agent event, named by the session and the pane
; it is about.

Library
[ signal_flow:[ Address HerdrRoute HerdrSessionName StartRejection ] ]
[ HerdrUnread.[ ServerUnreachable PaneUnreadable ]
  FreshRefusal.[ ConfigurationUnread NoLayerModel Rejected.StartRejection Unsettled ]
  WakeRecovery.[ Terminal AwaitingPane.HerdrRoute AwaitingServer Reconcile Unresolved ]
  PaneId.String
  AgentPaneEvent.{ HerdrSessionName PaneId } ]
[ ; A refusal, read for what can recover it.
  ClassifiesWakeRefusal.[ recovery.[ WakeRecovery ] ]
  ; The event a pane awaiter reacts to.
  PaneEventing.[ pane_event.[ AgentPaneEvent ] ]
  ; Tries again every wake awaiting the event's pane; answers the metaflows
  ; it tried.
  WakesOnPaneEvent.[ wake_on_pane_event.{ [ PaneEventing ] [ Vector<Address> ] } ] ]
[]
